  "notes": "GRAMMAR:\n{封|ふう}じる is an ichidan verb. The older godan form {封|ふう}ずる also exists but is less common in modern usage.\n\nCOLLOCATIONS:\n- {封筒|ふうとう}を{封|ふう}じる — to seal an envelope\n- {口|くち}を{封|ふう}じる — to silence someone, to shut someone up\n- {記憶|きおく}を{封|ふう}じる — to seal away memories\n- {攻撃|こうげき}を{封|ふう}じる — to block an attack\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{塞|ふさ}ぐ means to block or close off a physical opening. {封印|ふういん}する means to seal away, often with a supernatural or dramatic connotation. {封|ふう}じる covers both physical sealing and figurative suppression.",
